<http://data.silknow.org/object/85c5c120-8d27-301e-9d57-1946259eb5a1/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Long scarf or towel, embroidered in coloured silks (blue, green, black, yellow, orange and pink) and silver thread, with drawn threadwork and silk fringe at either end and narrower border of embroidery along sides. Architectural motif in row of four at the ends representing a church or monastery, with tiny figures and trees alongside. Running motif of birds along each long side. There is also a motif of a double-headed eagle in the main field, surrounded by smaller birds."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/85c5c120-8d27-301e-9d57-1946259eb5a1> .

